    <decisions>
        <description>Practice-first accounts: the corporate parent already exists, so Create_Corporate_Parent is skipped and the parent was never added to the numbering list (only the practice got an ID). If the account has a parent that has no Corporate ID yet, add the parent to practiceAccounts before the line items so Set_IDs numbers it.</description>
        <name>Has_Existing_Parent_Without_ID</name>
        <label>Has Existing Parent Without ID</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Line_Items</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Existing_Parent_Needs_ID</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opp_Account.ParentId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opp_Account.Parent.Corporate_ID__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Seed_Existing_Corp_Into_Collection</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>In_Collection</name>
        <label>In Collection?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Add_to_Practice_Collection</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>practiceAccounts</leftValueReference>
                <operator>Contains</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>Line_Item_Loop.Assign_to_Practice__r.Id</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Line_Item_Loop</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>In_LabProd_Collection</name>
        <label>In LabProd Collection?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Add_LabProd_to_Practice_Collection</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>YesLabProd</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>practiceAccounts</leftValueReference>
                <operator>Contains</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>Loop_Lab_Prods.Practice_Account__c</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Loop_Lab_Prods</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Does this practice-level deal need a corporate account created above it? Scoped to Account_Level__c = Practice on purpose: a blank account could be a corporate or a standalone practice and the flow cannot tell, so it keeps today&#39;s behaviour.</description>
        <name>Needs_Corporate_Parent</name>
        <label>Needs a corporate parent?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Has_Existing_Parent_Without_ID</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - carry on unchanged</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_Create_Corp</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opp_Account.Account_Level__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Practice</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opp_Account.ParentId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opp_Account.Corporate_Parent_Account__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Create_Corporate_Parent</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes - practice with no corp above it</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Stamp Corp/Practice IDs for accounts related to this opportunity

2026-06-03: BN - Add lookup to LabProds to properly set IDs for Lab-Only accounts
2026-09-08: AP - B3: create a corporate parent account above a parentless practice-level deal at Closed Won, before the numbering flow can mislabel it. New corp is added to practiceAccounts so one Update_Accounts numbers both the corp and the practice.
2026-09-14: AP - Fixed B3 numbering not firing for new corps: removed the erroneous Generate_Account_Numbers__c = true assignment from Create_Corporate_Parent (it was defeating the before-save flow&#39;s false-to-true transition trigger). Stamp_ID in the existing Set_IDs loop now numbers the new corp correctly, same as it already did for practices.
2026-10-08: AP - Fix: when the opportunity&#39;s account already has a corporate parent with no Corporate ID (practice-first creation), add that parent to practiceAccounts (Has_Existing_Parent_Without_ID / Seed_Existing_Corp_Into_Collection) so Set_IDs numbers it. Previously only the practice was numbered. The create-at-close path is unchanged.</description>
